{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '/\"'^def main(/,/''^def /p'\"' /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/21897d95.py\"","aggregated_output":"def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Repaint regions from T-shaped control markers, erase the markers, and optionally rotate based on a color-9 L-marker.\n\n    Input structure:\n    - The grid is a mosaic of monochrome regions.\n    - Color 1 forms T-shaped control markers on region boundaries.\n    - Some controls use three singleton color-1 pixels around a colored center; that center is a literal replacement color.\n    - An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker triggers 90-degree rotation of the output.\n\n    Rule:\n    - For a color-1 T marker, the single stem points at the destination region to repaint.\n    - The two diagonal cells behind the stem identify the source region; the destination gets that source region's original color.\n    - For a colored-center T marker, the same stem identifies the destination, but the center color is the replacement.\n    - All marker cells are filled with the final color of the source-side region.\n    - A 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker controls rotation: ┐ (corner top-right) → CCW 90°, ┌ (corner top-left) → CW 90°.\n\n    Key insight:\n    - The stem chooses what changes, while the two diagonals behind the stem choose where the marker itself belongs.\n    \"\"\"\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n    out = _solve_unrotated(g)\n    l9 = _find_l9_orientation(g)\n    if l9 == 'top_right':\n        return np.rot90(out, 1)\n    if l9 == 'top_left':\n        return np.rot90(out, 3)\n    return out\n\n# --------------- generator (l9rot) ---------------\n\n# ── Tunable constants ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Canvas / region sizing\nGRID_SIZE_MAX = 30                          # max rows or cols\nMIN_REGION_CELLS = 6                        # per-spec minimum\nREGION_SIZE_FACTOR = 2.5                    # min_grid_dim = max(9, n_regions * this)\nREGION_COUNTS = [4, 5, 6, 7, 8]            # candidate region counts\nREGION_WEIGHTS = [3, 3, 3, 1, 1]           # sampling weights for REGION_COUNTS\n\n# Marker counts (spec: 4-8 total, 2-6 normal, 0-2 colored)\nMARKER_MIN = 4\nMARKER_MAX = 8\nNORMAL_MAX = 6\nCOLORED_MAX = 2\n\n# Color pool (all ARC colors except 1, which is reserved for T-marker cells)\nCOLOR_POOL = [c for c in range(10) if c != 1]\n\n# L9 rotation marker\nL9_PROBABILITY = 0.5                        # chance of placing a rotation marker\nL9_OFFSETS = {                              # 5-cell L offsets keyed by corner orientation\n    'top_right': [(0, 0), (0, -1), (0, -2), (1, 0), (2, 0)],\n    'top_left':  [(0, 0), (0,  1), (0,  2), (1, 0), (2, 0)],\n}\n\n# Generation retry budget\nSEED_ATTEMPTS = 200                         # tries to place n distinct region seeds\nGEN_RETRIES = 300                           # outer generate_input retry budget\n\n_DIRS = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]\n\n\n# ── Small geometry helpers ─────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ndef _get_bar(stem):\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
